{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Fleetwood Mac and the Creedence collection feel like natural next choices because I want melodic classic rock, consistent with my Cars and classic-rock listening.",
    "ABBA fits my enjoyment of familiar pop hits, while Christmas Portrait connects directly to my latest Christmas-album interaction."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Manilow's ballads and Patsy Cline's traditional country vocals do not fit the rock and folk-pop sound I want today, even though they are familiar older music.",
    "I would hesitate over another Simon and Garfunkel collection because it may repeat music I already have; titles without an identifiable artist leave me unsure whether I would enjoy them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in greatest-hits collections seems to have been taken as interest in almost any greatest-hits album, although the artist and sound matter more to me.",
    "Enjoying older music does not mean that ballads, country vocals, classic rock and folk-pop are interchangeable choices for my current mood."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My classic-rock and folk-pop listening matters more to today's choice than my broader willingness to listen to vocal pop, which is why Adele appeals without being my first pick.",
    "A familiar artist is appealing, but another compilation needs enough different songs to feel worthwhile after my earlier best-of interaction."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in familiar hits and seasonal music, but sometimes treated compilation format and musical era as stronger matches than sound or song overlap."
}"}
